---
import CaseStudy from '../../layouts/CaseStudy.astro';
---
<CaseStudy
  metaTitle="National Trust Carbon Impact Studies | Building Physics Case Study | Rubix MEP"
  metaDesc="Case study: first-of-its-kind carbon impact study at Coleton Fishacre and LZC feasibility studies across 25+ National Trust sites, supporting the Trust's net zero by 2030 pledge."
  name="National Trust Carbon Impact Studies"
  displayName="National Trust <span class='c-green'>Carbon</span> Impact Studies"
  heroImage="/assets/national-trust-photo.jpg"
  capsules={[
    { text: 'Heritage &middot; Building Physics' },
    { text: 'National Trust', alt: true },
    { text: 'UK-wide', alt: true }
  ]}
  lede="A first-of-its-kind <span class='c-green'>carbon</span> impact study at Coleton Fishacre, and detailed renewable and Low-to-Zero <span class='c-green'>Carbon</span> feasibility studies across more than 25 National Trust sites, in support of the Trust&rsquo;s pledge to reach net zero <span class='c-green'>carbon</span> by 2030."
  glance={[
    { n: 'National Trust', l: 'Client' },
    { n: '25+', l: 'Sites studied UK-wide' },
    { n: '2030', l: 'Net zero <span class="c-green">carbon</span> pledge' },
    { n: '5%', l: 'Annual CO<sub>2</sub> reduction KPI' },
    { n: 'First', l: 'Of its kind for the Trust' }
  ]}
  overview={[
    'The <b><span class="c-green">carbon</span> impact study for the Coleton Fishacre site</b> evaluated energy use and associated CO<sub>2</sub> emissions across existing and projected future scenarios. Detailed energy and <span class="c-green">carbon</span> analysis modelling was carried out for the site, <b>the first of its kind for the National Trust</b>, enabling their Commercial Projects team to establish a clear, defined route to minimum operational <span class="c-green">carbon</span> using a four-step approach.',
    'Alongside, Rubix MEP were commissioned to survey and carry out <b>detailed renewable and Low-to-Zero <span class="c-green">Carbon</span> (LZC) feasibility studies</b> across more than 25 existing National Trust sites, from Tyntesfield and Kedleston Hall to Cragside and Formby, focused on the Trust&rsquo;s Food &amp; Beverage offers as part of its 2030 <span class="c-green">carbon</span> neutrality pledge.',
    'Each study reviewed the existing site services infrastructure and evaluated passive design measures, energy efficiency improvements and potential renewable / LZC technologies, with solutions rationalised into <b>site-specific recommendations with energy savings and payback calculations</b>. Further <span class="c-green">carbon</span> impact studies are now planned and underway for multiple National Trust sites across the UK.'
  ]}
  images={[
    { src: '/assets/carbon-4-step-chart.jpg', alt: 'Four-step carbon reduction approach: chart of stepped reductions towards minimum operational carbon' },
    { src: '/assets/national-trust-photo.jpg', alt: 'National Trust property served by the carbon impact studies programme' }
  ]}
  quote={{
    text: 'Having worked with Rubix on a number of our projects I was confident in bringing them in as our in-house M&amp;E consultant for hospitality projects. This has proved to be a good decision as Rubix have shown themselves to be thorough, detailed, prompt and at all times highly professional.',
    by: 'Matthew Knowles',
    org: 'National Trust Senior Programme Manager, F&B'
  }}
  scope={[
    { h: 'Site-wide <span class="c-green">carbon</span> modelling', p: 'Detailed energy and <span class="c-green">carbon</span> analysis modelling at Coleton Fishacre, establishing a defined four-step route to minimum operational <span class="c-green">carbon</span> against the Trust&rsquo;s 5% annual CO<sub>2</sub> reduction KPI.' },
    { h: 'LZC feasibility studies', p: 'Renewable and Low-to-Zero <span class="c-green">Carbon</span> feasibility studies across 25+ sites, appraising passive design, energy efficiency and renewable technologies with payback calculations.' },
    { h: 'F&amp;B design delivery', p: 'The Trust&rsquo;s F&amp;B MEP design guide, plus delivered schemes including the first F&amp;B solar PV installation at Emmetts Garden Tea Rooms and the Grade II listed Tyntesfield Cow Barn refurbishment.' }
  ]}
  chipsLabel="Sites include"
  chips={['Coleton Fishacre', 'Tyntesfield', 'Kedleston Hall', 'Cragside', 'Anglesey Abbey', 'Formby', 'Emmetts Garden', '+ 18 more']}
